PART 5 -- MASS SPLIT AND JACKKNIFE: does the answer come from the sample or from a few objects?
==============================================================================================================================
  low  V_flat (V_flat <= 106.3 km/s): N =  1119, a_0 = 3.0480e-11 (-0.487 dex canon), Upsilon = 0.432, conditioning dI/dlog a_0 = -4.750e-12
  high V_flat (V_flat > 106.3 km/s): N =  2021, a_0 = 9.9114e-11 (+0.025 dex canon), Upsilon = 0.473, conditioning dI/dlog a_0 = -5.791e-12
  leave-one-galaxy-out: largest single-galaxy influence +0.1619 dex (CamB); rms 0.0137 dex over 147 galaxies
  [FAIL] 5A no single galaxy carries the measurement (bug pattern: an answer that is one object)   (largest leave-one-out shift +0.1619 dex (CamB))
  [FAIL] 5B ⚠ THE MASS SPLIT IS THE CHECK THAT CAN REALLY FAIL: one acceleration scale must give the same a_0 in low-mass and high-mass discs.  Reported whichever way it comes out   (low V_flat 3.048e-11 vs high V_flat 9.911e-11 = +0.512 dex apart)

==============================================================================================================================
PART 6 -- THE NEWTONIAN ALTERNATIVE, AND CONTROLS
==============================================================================================================================
  Newton (nu = 1): g_bar^req = g_obs and a_0 has DISAPPEARED from the estimator -- there is no free
  parameter left to drive the intercept to zero, which is the whole statement.  What it leaves is a
  forced intercept of 1.7235e-11 +- 1.34e-12 m/s^2 (12.8 sigma from the zero the baryon
  decomposition requires) -- an acceleration every disc needs that its own baryons do not supply.  Its
  size is 0.18 a_0 (canonical) / 0.15 a_0 (alt).  The stellar slope it forces is
  0.646 against the kernel's 0.604.
  [PASS] 6A THE NEWTONIAN ALTERNATIVE IS COMPUTED BESIDE AND FAILS IN THE SAME REGRESSION: with no boost there is no a_0 to solve for, and the intercept the baryon decomposition requires to be zero is not zero.  This check fails if Newton can satisfy the intercept condition after all   (forced intercept 1.724e-11 +- 1.34e-12 m/s^2 = 12.8 sigma from zero, i.e. 0.18 a_0 canonical / 0.15 a_0 alt)
  injection: a_0 9.360e-11, Upsilon 0.500 -> recovered a_0 9.361e-11 (+0.0000 dex), Upsilon 0.5000
  injection: a_0 1.130e-10, Upsilon 0.500 -> recovered a_0 1.130e-10 (+0.0000 dex), Upsilon 0.5000
  injection: a_0 3.744e-10, Upsilon 0.500 -> recovered a_0 3.744e-10 (+0.0000 dex), Upsilon 0.5000
  [PASS] 6B INJECTION: the estimator must return both the injected a_0 AND the injected Upsilon   (a_0 +0.0000 dex, Upsilon 0.5000 against the injected 0.500)
  [PASS] 6C MUTATION: a 4x wrong a_0 must come back 4x wrong   (+0.0000 dex from the injected 4x canonical)
  mutation: scrambling which point's stellar term goes with which g_obs -> a_0 1.081e-10 (+0.433 dex), Upsilon 0.000
  [PASS] 6D MUTATION: destroying the pairing between the stellar term and g_obs must wreck the Upsilon the regression returns -- if a scrambled sample still gave a stellar-population M/L the regression would be measuring nothing   (scrambled Upsilon 0.000 against the real 0.604)

==============================================================================================================================
VERDICT ON K3b
==============================================================================================================================
  a_0 = 3.9853e-11 +- 0.113 dex (galaxy bootstrap) +- 0.569 dex (weighting systematic)
      = -0.371 dex from canonical, -0.453 dex from alt.
  Upsilon_[3.6] = 0.604 (range 0.498-0.620 across weightings).
  d log a_0/d log Upsilon = +0.0e+00 EXACTLY; d log a_0/d log D = -1.51.
  IS_RESTATEMENT = True.  It is v^4 = G M_b a_0 rearranged, and the method is credited to
  Stark, McGaugh & Schombert 2009.  It is a bookkeeping improvement on a published method, not a new law,
  and it must be described that way.

RESULT: 14 checks, 2 FAIL -> ['5A no single galaxy carries the measurement (bug pattern: an answer that is one object)', '5B ⚠ THE MASS SPLIT IS THE CHECK THAT CAN REALLY FAIL: one acceleration scale must give the same a_0 in low-mass and high-mass discs.  Reported whichever way it comes out']   rc=1
